 "J02": {
  "dur": 30.98125,
  "text": "Quick fix on one word. When blood pressure drops as you stand up, it's called orthostatic hypotension. Hypo means low. You get up, your pressure falls, and you may feel dizzy or even faint. Doctor check. That's why a doctor may check your blood pressure sitting and standing. So, with falls in the picture, should older people be treated at all?",
