 "U01": {
  "dur": 38.2955,
  "text": "One point needs a little more detail. Diuretics, often called water tablets, aren't automatically off-limits for older adults. In fact, the HIVET trial in people aged 80 and over used one and aimed for 150 over 80. Today, there's no single target for everyone. Doctors also weigh dizziness, frailty, kidney function, and other conditions. Even some prostate medicines can make blood pressure drop when you stand.",
